  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [tabindex-ordered focus navigation scope](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#tabindex-ordered-focus-navigation-scope) step seems to explicitly exclude [focus navigation scope owners](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#focus-navigation-scope-owner) with a negative tabindex. My read of this is that opening a popover with a trigger with a negative tabindex should not add the popover contents to the taborder.\n\nAcross browsers, Tab does move focus into the popover. (I think this is desired, but not per spec).\n\nAfter the focus leaves the popover, browsers behave differently. Chromium keeps the popover contents in the taborder, and Webkit/Firefox remove the popover contents from the taborder. \n\nHere's a reproduction- https://codepen.io/editor/jamessw/pen/01a1ef32-8a51-799a-b5fc-deeb8af9c0fb",
